# "universal" occurs in S1 ("universal happiness", happiness of everyone) and in S2 ("universal rules", rules holding without exception), but neither use is a claim used in more than one statement, so no claim changes sense.
# general_only keeps the contrast general (holds on average) vs universal (holds always) the same way in P2 and P3; P3 restates it as "always and necessarily", which is the same sense.
